  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: 24-hour reporting for all incidents, immediate customer notice for ongoing risks. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 5% trigger for regulator review, but no automatic sales ban; customers receive numeric failure rates. S3 requires new units to have shut-off and retrofits within 6 years with feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in suppression within 36 months. S5 makes recall discretionary based on regulator determination, with an 8/100k review trigger."
